  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "A best practice is to include the charset meta definition in a HTML page, but this is missing in the maintenance notice shown on VRChat Wiki at https://wiki.vrchat.com/ during a maintenance.\n\nExpected markup: `<meta charset=\"utf-8\">` inside the `<head>` element, placed on line immediately before or after the `<title>` element (but within the first 1024 bytes of the document).\n\nActual markup: Missing.\n\nSee:\n\n- https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTML/Reference/Elements/meta#charset\n\n- https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/semantics.html#charset\n\nNote: The charset must be `charset=\"utf-8\"`, not `charset=\"UTF-8\"`! The RFC 3629 standard name is a hyphenated UTF-8, but the web markup is lowercase hyphenated.",
